cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the paper."
title: "Feedback-Learning-Based Polarimetric Scattering Representation for PolSAR Ship Detection"
abstract: >-
  Code and result tables for a feedback-learning pipeline for PolSAR ship
  detection. A multilayer-perceptron teacher converts pixel-level hard labels
  into continuous ship membership, and a symbolic-regression search fits a
  closed-form polarimetric descriptor under an accuracy-complexity trade-off.
  The repository covers the complexity-6 and complexity-29 descriptors, the
  eight-detector comparison, the pixel-level and target-to-clutter analyses,
  the soft-label and operator-set ablations, the two-layer box refinement, and
  the zero-training transfer to IPSD with one scalar calibration.
